-- title:
--   Quotient by cᵢXᵢ+Xᵢ^{Nᵢ}, cᵢ nilpotent, is free of rank prod Nᵢ
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a nontrivial commutative ring, let $g$ be a natural number, let $N : \mathrm{Fin}\,g \to \mathbb{N}$ assign an exponent $N_i$ to each index, and let $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,g \to R$ assign to each index an element $c_i$ of $R$ which is assumed nilpotent. Consider the ring $R[[X_i : i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,g]]$ of formal power series in $g$ variables over $R$ and the ideal generated by the set of the $g$ series $C(c_i)\,X_i + X_i^{N_i}$, that is, the span of the range of the map $i \mapsto C(c_i)\cdot X_i + X_i^{N_i}$, where $C$ denotes the inclusion of constants. The assertion is threefold, for the quotient of $R[[X_1,\dots,X_g]]$ by this ideal viewed as an $R$-module: it is a free $R$-module; it is a finite (finitely generated) $R$-module; and its rank, in the sense of `Module.finrank` over $R$, equals the product $\prod_{i} N_i$. No positivity hypothesis is imposed on the $N_i$: if some $N_i = 0$ the corresponding generator is $1 + c_iX_i$, the ideal is the whole ring, and both sides of the rank equality vanish; for $g = 0$ the empty product gives rank $1$.
--
--   This is a Weierstrass-type division statement: each generator $X_i^{N_i} + c_iX_i$ is distinguished in the variable $X_i$, being monic of degree $N_i$ with nilpotent lower coefficient, so that the monomials $X^{\alpha}$ with $\alpha_i < N_i$ form an $R$-basis of the quotient, generalising the case $c = 0$ where the box of monomials is visibly a basis. It is used in the construction of formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules entering the Cerednik–Drinfeld setting, where it supplies the freeness and the height computation for the relevant quotients.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_free_and_finite_and_finrank_quotient_span_range_C_mul_X_add_X_pow_of_isNilpotent.lean

